tags.value:
@remarks
If the message meets the log level threshold, the provided data will be
merged with any existing data on the log entry.

@remarks
This emitter captures the formatted output in a public `output` property
instead of writing to a destination, allowing for easy inspection in tests.

tags.doc:
```typescript
const tb = new TextBuilder(CustomMsgBuilder);
tb.line.text('Hello').value('world');
tb.newline();
tb.line.plain('Done');
console.log(tb.emit());
